{"legislative_session": "20252026", "identifier": "AB2030", "title": "Dietary supplements for weight loss and over-the-counter diet pills.", "from_organization": "~{\"classification\": \"lower\"}", "classification": ["bill"], "subject": ["Dietarysupplementsforweightlossandover-the-counterdietpills"], "abstracts": [{"note": "summary", "abstract": "Existing law regulates the safety of various consumer products, including, among other things, specific additives in foods, chemicals in products for young children, and lead in tableware.\n\nThis bill would prohibit a person from selling, offering to sell, or giving away as either a retail or wholesale promotion, and a delivery seller from selling, delivering, or causing to be delivered, an over-the-counter diet pill or dietary supplement for weight loss or muscle building, as defined, to any person in this state under 18 years of age, except as specified, by requiring a specified identification check. The bill would make a person who violates these provisions liable for a civil penalty of no more than $500 for each violation, as specified, and would authorize the Attorney General, a county counsel, or a city attorney to apply to a court for, and would authorize that court to have jurisdiction upon hearing and for cause shown to grant, a temporary or permanent injunction enjoining or restraining any person or entity from violating any of the prohibitions. The bill would make a prevailing plaintiff in an action under these provisions entitled to an award of reasonable attorney's fees and costs."}], "other_titles": [], "other_identifiers": [{"identifier": "ocd-bill-ca-20252026-ab2030"}], "actions": [{"description": "Read first time. To print.", "date": "2026-02-17", "organization_id": "~{\"classification\": \"lower\"}", "classification": ["reading-1"], "related_entities": []}, {"description": "From printer. May be heard in committee March 20.", "date": "2026-02-18", "organization_id": "~{\"classification\": \"lower\"}", "cla